        "semantic_summary": "Run one jq filter against a local JSON file and return parsed or raw output\nDirect jq argv execution for ordinary non-option filter strings over one local JSON file; not safe jq option isolation, filter sandboxing, JSON file mutation, guaranteed structured multi-result collection, schema validation, or generic shell execution.\nDirectly invokes the argv vector `[\"jq\", jq_filter, file_path]` with the filter defaulting to `.`. There is no `--` option terminator, so a value beginning with `-` can be interpreted by jq as a command-line option rather than a filter. The wrapper parses stdout only when the entire stream is one non-null JSON document.\nDeclared result: json | JSON execution envelope containing a single parsed jq JSON value when possible, otherwise raw jq stdout, plus exit and stderr metadata.",
