        "semantic_limitations": [
          "modify overwrite or persist changes to a JSON file",
          "guarantee a structured array for multiple jq output values",
          "pass jq command-line options safely",
          "validate JSON against a schema or execute arbitrary shell commands",
          "passes `[jq, jq_filter, file_path]` directly with no `--` option terminator; a jq_filter beginning with `-` may be consumed as an option such as `--version`, so command-line options or option-looking filters cannot be passed safely",
          "multiple jq output values are not collected into an array and remain raw stdout with result=null; a single JSON null is also returned as result=null with `null\\n` retained because the helper uses None as both the parsed value and no-parse sentinel",
          "jq false or null results still use jq's default exit behavior because `-e` is absent; consumers must inspect result rather than assume truthiness from exit 0",
          "jq programs can read changing process state through builtins such as `now`, `env`, and `$ENV`, so output is not deterministic; the wrapper does not sandbox filters, has a fixed 120-second timeout, applies no output-size truncation, and does not modify the source file"
        ],
        "semantic_summary": "Run one jq filter against a local JSON file and return parsed or raw output\nDirect jq argv execution for ordinary non-option filter strings over one local JSON file; not safe jq option isolation, filter sandboxing, JSON file mutation, guaranteed structured multi-result collection, schema validation, or generic shell execution.\nDirectly invokes the argv vector `[\"jq\", jq_filter, file_path]` with the filter defaulting to `.`. There is no `--` option terminator, so a value beginning with `-` can be interpreted by jq as a command-line option rather than a filter. The wrapper parses stdout only when the entire stream is one non-null JSON document.\nDeclared result: json | JSON execution envelope containing a single parsed jq JSON value when possible, otherwise raw jq stdout, plus exit and stderr metadata.",
